Stage 9 code is non-interactive. Complete these operator-owned activities
without editing broker source; provide values through `lz-config.json` and the
environment variables below.

## Before broker apply

- [ ] Review `tenant-readiness-report.md` and resolve every blocking discovery
  finding, or document an approved exception before using
  `LZ_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOW_NOT_READY=true`.
- [ ] Authenticate Azure CLI to tenant
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:azure.tenantId}}` with permission to manage app registrations,
  service principals, federated credentials, subscription RBAC, and the selected
  backend.
- [ ] Authenticate GitHub CLI to
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.repositorySlug}}` with repository administration,
  Actions variable, environment, and branch-protection access.
- [ ] Confirm the default branch is
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.defaultBranch}}`.
- [ ] Review the exact plan:
  `pwsh ./bootstrap-broker.ps1` (plan-only by default).
- [ ] Confirm every planned identity is repo-scoped and no OIDC subject contains
  a wildcard.

#{{IF computed.backendIsHcp}}
## HCP Terraform

- [ ] Export `TFE_TOKEN` from a secure secret source. Do not put it in
  `lz-config.json`, shell history, generated output, or Terraform variables.
- [ ] Confirm HCP organization
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:backend.hcpTerraform.organization}}` and workspace prefix
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:backend.hcpTerraform.workspacePrefix}}`.
#{{ELSE}}
## Azure Storage backend

- [ ] Confirm the backend subscription, resource group, storage account, and
  container names are approved and globally unique where required.
- [ ] Confirm the operator can create the backend resources and data-plane
  container using Entra authentication.
#{{ENDIF}}

## Apply

- [ ] Set `LZ_CONFIG_PATH` to the exported `lz-config.json`.
- [ ] Set `LZ_DISCOVERY_PATH` to `discovery-inventory.json`.
- [ ] Set `LZ_BOOTSTRAP_OUTPUT` to a protected local output directory.
- [ ] Set `LZ_BOOTSTRAP_APPLY=true`.
- [ ] Run `./bootstrap-broker.sh` or
  `pwsh ./bootstrap-broker.ps1 -Apply`.
- [ ] Preserve `bootstrap-plan.json` and `bootstrap-audit.json` as change
  evidence; neither file contains access tokens.

## Required live verification

- [ ] Read back every Entra application, service principal, RBAC assignment,
  issuer, audience, and exact subject.
- [ ] Run the generated Azure OIDC verification workflow and confirm a real
  `pull_request` token exchange succeeds with the read-only plan identity.
- [ ] Confirm apply identities can be assumed only through their matching
  `environment:<name>` subject.
- [ ] Confirm GitHub environments and variables exist for:
#{{FOREACH env IN computed.allEnvironments}}
  - [ ] `{{FACTORY-RAW:env}}`
#{{ENDFOREACH}}
- [ ] Confirm `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.defaultBranch}}` protection requires
  the comma-separated checks in `LZ_REQUIRED_STATUS_CHECKS` (defaults to
  `qlty check`), linear history, pull-request review, and blocks force pushes
  and deletion.
- [ ] Confirm backend workspaces/storage and state-lock behavior.
- [ ] Review `bootstrap-audit.json`; resolve every
  `pendingUserActivities` entry.

## Values never stored in configuration

- Azure user/device login tokens.
- GitHub user/device login tokens.
- `TFE_TOKEN`.
- Any client secret or storage access key.
